Wrong rhetoric

    adverse rhetoric!! ‘evidences’ at the outset seeming to premise the conclusion
        : see @ text.brec
    false rhetoric!! the artificial explanantia are as indeterminate as the natural
        : see @ text.brec
    - the foregoing flags suggest that I entered my rhetoric on the wrong foot
    restart+ on the right foot
        ' (2) discovery of coinciding ends in (discoveries of) ground and safehold is *the* crux
          and place to start
            : re `(coincid)ing ends` see `a.+surprising.+larger ${same}ence` @ ._/text.notes.brec
            : note : notepad entry 2026-9-8a
        ' (1) mere supposition (e.g. 8i) that there *could* be a (valid) reason (viz. ground) to reach
          for the safehold (as every fibre of my being beckons) suffices, for it hypothesizes
          what would be a startling coincidence of ends and means
            : note : notepad entry 2026-9-8b
        ' (3) that coincidence would suffice as a reason to believe that a truth of *practical* logic
          (of the ground) was somehow the cause of the safehold, which it could only (plausibly) be
          through action, specifically an act of creation, implying therefore a creator —
          This gives me reason to believe in a creator of some sort, and now I have (without
          needing to go into speculation re the sort of creator) all I need to ground an ethic
            : note : notepad entry 2026-9-8c
        ' (ad 8b) ‘My introduction to practical philosophy is the cosmic safehold. “Why should we
          … to carry on indefinitely … {as it promises to allow}?  To what end?” I ask,
          and {…opens before me}|{[the] answers begin to come}.’
              The key to this field is the question, a question one can keep repeating until … {one can
          repeat it no longer, and then …} or seemingly without end, indefinitely.  {Note that,
          for it is surprising.} {But then think, think what is promised, what it would mean
          if this practical logic that we query truly *held* an answer to this question.}
            : note : notepad entry 2026-9-8i
        ' ‘Our entry to practical and moral philosophy is the cosmic safehold, and [y]our key [to it] is
          the question, “To what end?”’  [So {maybe} including the reader to whom I might pose questions,
          or better, to whom I might give answers, the roles being reversed and I becoming|being
          convinced of the reader’s argument.]  Yet clarity above all, and here apropos of the metaphor:
          ‘I {could hardly|not}|cannot contemplate the prospect of entering the safehold without [asking]
          that question, nor make headway in[to] the philosophy without {insisting on a valid} |
          {[contemplating] the prospect of an} answer [to it] [*in that context*].’
            : note : notepad entry 2026-9-9a
            : ad `that context` : viz. the context in which the question was posed,
              literally that of ‘the prospect of entering the safehold’
        ' {the full question (8i)} … ‘repeat, repeat,’ “seemingly without end, *indefinitely* …” (8i)
          ‘But that is not how the key works.  Rather {“think, think”}.  That is the way. —
          For this one|we|I|you need a proven answer.’
            : note : notepad entry 2026-9-9b
