        salvage: meaning from under the metaphor of an entry key
            : re `metaphor of.+(entry) (key)`
              viz. `^*' ‘Our.+${1}.+is.+the.+safehold, .+our.+${2}.+is the question, “To what end\?”’`sp
            ● necessity of the question
                = (causal-theoretic) to satisfy reason’s urging
                = (technical-practical) to discover a method of answering
                    : re `to (discover) (a method.+)$` e.g. `^*⇒ ${1}y of one$` @ `^*─ ${2}$`
                / causing:
            ⇒ the prospect of (the value of) [having] an answer (in the context of the safehold)
                : re `an answer.+` viz. `^*⇒ the fact of ${same}`
                / causing:
            ⇒ the fact of the question
                / causing:
            ─ a method of answering
                ⇒ discovery of one
                    / causing:
                ⇒ its application
                    = analysis of the question
                / causing:
            ⇒ the fact of an answer (in the context of the safehold)
                / causing:
            ⇒ discovery of an ethic grounded and in effect
            ' Thus (1) the metaphoric introduction and prospect (9a) through to looking at the aetiology
              and the design explanantia (their indeterminate reasons echoing the [very] same question)
              with the promise thereby of mining further philosophic answers and ultimately grounding
              an ethic, and then (2) the method (9b,c) summarized and directly employed.
                : note : notepad entry 2026-9-10a
